# Graphify is for the text/code "second brain" (architecture, how things
# connect) - never for transcribing video or vision-extracting images.
# Locked in 2026-08-03 after the Video Editor domain build attempt hit
# 979 files / 7.8M words, almost entirely binary production media.
# Re-confirmed 2026-09-04 (Tony): images and video are NEVER graphified —
# any extension, any filename, any letter-case — no exceptions.
#
# CASE-INSENSITIVE ON PURPOSE: graphify's own `_is_ignored()` uses Python's
# fnmatch, which is case-SENSITIVE on macOS/Linux (fnmatch only case-folds on
# Windows) — a plain `*.png` line does NOT match `photo.PNG`. Confirmed live
# 2026-09-04: 007_Resource_Library's corpus detect() returned 784 "image"
# files despite `*.png`/`*.jpg` being listed, because nearly all of them were
# `.PNG`. Every extension below uses a [xX] bracket per letter so it matches
# any case combination (.png/.PNG/.Png/...), not just an explicit uppercase
# twin — more robust than listing both cases by hand.

# Images (any case)
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[sS][vV][gG]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[hH][eE][iI][fF]
*.[iI][cC][oO]
*.[aA][vV][iI][fF]

# Video (any case)
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[mM]4[vV]
*.[wW][mM][vV]
*.[fF][lL][vV]
*.[mM][pP][gG]
*.[mM][pP][eE][gG]
*.3[gG][pP]

# Audio (any case) — kept from the original list, extended for consistency
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[wW][aA][vV]
*.[mM]4[aA]
*.[aA][aA][cC]
